    "title": "Tracking late-night storms and much cooler air - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zack Webster ,\n1 days ago SYNOPSIS – We finally didn’t tie or break a record high for the first time in five days yesterday, but we’ll continue to stay dry and warm with partly sunny to partly cloudy skies through much of the day today. That will once again warm those temperatures back up to near-record values. A line of scattered showers and thunderstorms will bring some rain and gusty winds to portions of the region later tonight, then much cooler and much more seasonable air finally moves into the region for Thanksgiving and Black Friday before we start turning gradually warmer again through the weekend. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
